# Build context hygiene for Dockerfile / Dockerfile.gateway / Dockerfile.operator.
#
# Each image does `COPY . .` to get the Go tree, which without this file ships
# the WHOLE repository -- 4.9 GB, of which research/ alone is 4.4 GB of
# measurement artifacts and eval/results/ is 426 MB of soak evidence. The
# gateway build spent over a minute transferring context before compiling a
# line. None of it is needed: the builder wants go.mod, go.sum and the Go
# sources, nothing else.
#
# Dockerfile.gateway carried the note "NOT VERIFIED LOCALLY: Docker is not
# installed on the development machine", which is how a 4.9 GB context went
# unnoticed -- the image had never actually been built here until now.

# Version control and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Measurement artifacts and generated records -- never inputs to a build
research/
eval/results/
reproduce_out/
benchmarks/
artifacts/
data/
thesis/
docs/

# Local build outputs and databases
*.exe
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.csv.gz
*.log

# Python/eval side of the repo: not part of any Go image
eval/
scripts/
infra/
deploy/
